                 core3h - general Core3H board communication

  Syntax:     coreh3=n,data_to

  Response:   core3h/n,data_from


Settable parameters:
  n           Core3H board number, 1-8
  data_to     Complete message to be sent to Core3H board; no checking is
              performed.

Monitor-only parameters:
  data_from   response of Core3H board, if any.

Comments:

This command sends a low-level communication message to a Core3H board and
presents the response. The response may span multiple lines corresponding to
the lines sent by the Core3H board. All lines except the final one will be
labeled as '#dbbcn#dbbc3/' without the board number. The final response line
will include the FiLa10G prompt (which is what the Core3H board returns).

Communication with the Core3H board is accomplished through the DBBC3. The
user should not put 'core3h=n,' at the start of the 'data_to' field as the
command will do this automatically.

The 'core3h' command cannot be used if the rack type in 'equip.ctl' specifies a
'dbbc' (DBBC2) type. Other rack types do not limit the use of this command.
